  "experiment": "H1.20-action-admissibility-diagnostic-v1",
  "question": "Does hiding a retrieved recovery action when it is not admissible in the current state recover the usability lost by raw text memory?",
  "hypothesis": "Raw text memory often carries a recorded action that is absent from the current Allowed actions list. Replacing only that action field with a state-only notice should improve valid completion and qualified-positive rate relative to raw text memory.",
